<li>I'm not sure I could summarize it without taking up at least as much space as the article itself.</li>
<li>The fact that it is/they are (very slowly) learning.</li>
<li>The word choice of 'thrall'.</li>
<li>3242, or whatever is responsible for it, coming across as basically just as clueless as we are. Like, fantastic dark humor with Floppy Disk Y's moment of &quot;The new person you gave us asked us to send you a message! Here it is: AAAAAHHHH&quot;</li>
<li>Everything else.</li>
</ul>
<p>Yeah I just really like this article. Looking forward to reading it again tomorrow and trying to connect more of the pieces. In fact, I suspect it'll be true for a while that every reread will feel rewarding. Seriously, bravo.</p>

